  "summary": "The allies stood behind the Spree at Bautzen in a fortified line along the heights. On the first day Napoleon forced the river and took the town; on the second he pinned the allied centre and left while Ney's and Lauriston's corps marched round the right. Barclay's Russians and Kleist's Prussians held them off long enough round Gleina and Preititz, and when Ney, unsure of his orders, halted instead of driving on to the allies' rear, Wittgenstein and Blücher got their armies away to the east.",
